        <p class="eyebrow">The pathway</p>
        <h2>Five steps from first conversation to first patient</h2>
        <p>No two international doctors follow exactly the same route. Where you trained, your specialty and how recently you&rsquo;ve practised all shape what&rsquo;s required. We map it out with you at the start, then manage every step through to approval.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">1</div><h4>Map your pathway</h4><p>We assess your qualifications, specialty and recent practice to identify the right AHPRA or MCNZ registration pathway and give you a clear plan.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">2</div><h4>Secure your role</h4><p>Already have a job offer? We support the applications linked to your new role. If not, <a href="https://wave.com.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wavelength&rsquo;s medical recruitment team</a> can help you find one.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">3</div><h4>Registration and college applications</h4><p>We prepare and review your registration and specialist college applications, coordinate Primary Source Verification and handle any further requests.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">4</div><h4>Lodge your visa</h4><p>Our registered migration agents manage your Skills in Demand (subclass 482), Employer Nomination Scheme (subclass 186) or other visa, including visas for eligible family members.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">5</div><h4>Set up Medicare</h4><p>You&rsquo;ll generally need a provider number for each practice location. We manage the application and advise on any restrictions or exemptions, including section 19AB.</p></div>
      </div>
